<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-KEB kangaroo bond set at 40 bp over.</title>
<headline>RTRS-KEB kangaroo bond set at 40 bp over.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Korea Exchange Bank's A$180 million kangaroo bond has been priced at 40 basis points over the mid-rate of the Australian Treasury July 1999 bonds, lead manager Bankers Trust Australia.</p>
<p>The bonds, which carry a coupon of 6.75 percent, mature on December 15, 1999. Kangaroo bonds are issued by foreign borrowers in the Australian domestic bond market.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
